CVE-2026-42198 (GHSA-98qh-xjc8-98pq) and CVE-2026-54291: force postgresql 42.7.12 against Quarkus BOM overrides.
https://github.com/pgjdbc/pgjdbc/security/advisories/GHSA-98qh-xjc8-98pq
Vert.x stays on Quarkus 3.37 BOM 4.5.28 (includes CVE-2026-6860 fix from 4.5.27).
diff --git a/servers/quarkus-server/build.gradle.kts b/servers/quarkus-server/build.gradle.kts
--- a/servers/quarkus-server/build.gradle.kts
+++ b/servers/quarkus-server/build.gradle.kts
@@ -30,6 +30,19 @@
 
 publishingHelper { mavenName = "Nessie - Quarkus Server" }
 
+// CVE-2026-42198 (GHSA-98qh-xjc8-98pq) is a pgjdbc SCRAM-SHA-256 handshake CPU-exhaustion DoS,
+// and CVE-2026-54291 is a channel-binding downgrade on channelBinding=require connections. Both
+// are fixed in 42.7.12. The Quarkus platform BOM can still constrain pgjdbc to an older release,
+// so force the resolved jar to 42.7.12 so the fast-jar packaging and the SBOM/Scout scan reflect
+// the fixed version. Vert.x stays on the Quarkus 3.37 BOM at 4.5.28; do not force vert.x 5.x here.
+configurations.configureEach {
+  resolutionStrategy {
+    force(
+      "org.postgresql:postgresql:42.7.12",
+    )
+  }
+}
+
 // CVE-2026-45292 (GHSA-rcgg-9c38-7xpx): unbounded memory allocation in
 // OpenTelemetry W3C baggage propagation, fixed in 1.62.0+. libs.versions.toml
 // declares opentelemetry 1.63.0, but the Quarkus platform BOM can still constrain
